 -- Shadowfetch Project <signing@shadowfetch.com>  Thu, 09 Jul 2026 14:10:00 -0400

shadowfetch-themes (1.7.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * "Agent Ready" release - run a real autonomous AI agent on your own machine:
    - Explicit choice of agent: Hermes (Nous Research's self-improving agent) or
      OpenClaw, each set up in a single command. A new 'shadowfetch-agents' front
      door and an "AI Agents - Get Started" menu entry walk you through it, and the
      first-run Welcome wizard offers the same choice.
    - Agent install guide shipped both in the OS
      (/usr/share/doc/shadowfetch/AGENTS.md) and on the website (/linux/agents),
      covering Hermes, OpenClaw and running everything 100% locally via Ollama.
    - Agent-ready prerequisites baked in: Node.js, Python 3.13, git, ripgrep,
      ffmpeg and now pipx, so agents install fast and offline-friendly.
    - OpenClaw now actually runs out of the box: it needs Node 22+ (Debian ships
      Node 20), so the helper provisions Node 22 LTS into your user account - no
      root, system Node untouched - then installs and verifies it before launch.
  * Stability and debug pass (broad audit, adversarially verified):
    - Build fix: 'wsdd' was dropped from Debian trixie; replaced with 'wsdd2'.
    - No more 'degraded' boot: snapper-cleanup.timer is enabled only when a btrfs
      snapshot config exists, instead of unconditionally on live/non-btrfs systems.
    - Wi-Fi: rfkill-unblock and regulatory-domain services now fire on the very
      first boot rather than one boot late.
    - Hardening: a locally-installed Ollama is pinned to localhost by a shipped
      systemd drop-in, not only by the setup helper.
    - Polish: branded menu icons for the agent tools, de-staled website roadmap
      and verify pages, and the duplicate agent-picker menu entry retired.

